WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.610
In this video, I'll answer the questions
I get asked most often when I first speak

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:08.280
to a founder. So you get a clear picture
of what I actually do, who it's for, and

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.980
how it works. And you can decide for
yourself whether it's right for you before

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:17.900
we even get on the call. I work with
founder-led businesses, usually somewhere

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.880
between 1 and 25 million in revenue.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.240
They've grown well, but the owner is
still the one approving most things.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.930
So if the important decisions still come
back to you, if your team waits for your

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.830
input before they act, and if you couldn't
step away for 2 or 3 weeks without things

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.000
starting to slip, this is for you.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.760
What I usually see is a business that's
past the early stage, but the way it's run

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.240
hasn't caught up with how big it's got.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.090
That's where I come in. You lead the
change, and I work alongside you to build

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:48.370
the systems and processes that let your
team run the day-to-day, so you can get

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.340
back to strategy. There
are a few signs I look for.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:58.730
The first is decisions, if the ones that
should sit with your team still land on

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:04.050
your desk, that's a sign. The second is
where your processes live, if they hunt

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:08.080
people's heads or scatter across documents
and nobody could pick one up and follow

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.770
it, that's another. The third is that if
you've already tried to fix it, maybe you

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:17.330
hired someone or brought in some software
and the chaos underneath is still the

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:21.600
same. And the last one is when the same
problems keep coming back, month after

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.600
month, because nothing
stops them at the source.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.580
None of this is about ability. It's what
happens when a business outgrows the way

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.400
of working that got it off the ground.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.060
Most growing businesses hit this stage.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.200
The founders will move past it, other ones
will build a structure to replace it, and

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.500
that's what we'll work on together.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.460
I don't use the word "coaching".

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.900
Coaching tends to be about
mindset and accountability.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.300
Someone asking you good questions
but never getting their hands dirty.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.220
Traditional consulting is the other end.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:55.530
Someone hands you a framework or does it
work for you and the minute they leave,

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.540
nothing sticks, because your
team never learned to run it.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.510
What I do sits in between. You get
structure, the challenge and the

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:06.340
accountability, but you also get
real systems and hands on hell.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:10.160
And you and your team build it into the
business yourselves, with me alongside

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.140
you, so it's still there
long after we've finished.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.780
That's why I call it advisory. With you.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.220
I'm not going to come in and take over
your operations, but I'm not going to hand

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.860
you a plan and disappear either.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:27.540
I've seen founders given a polished
framework and then left alone to make it

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.140
work. That's not how I do
it. The systems are yours.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.470
You and your team build them in, and
I'm right there with you, because

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:38.140
implementation is the hard part,
and it's where most people give up.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:38.140
Depending on where you are at, I might
spend time on site early on, and I stay

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:38.140
with you through the engagement
until the systems are actually

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:45.460
running.

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:51.520
Not just written down. Depends on where
you are starting from, your team and how

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.540
disciplined you are about doing the work.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.380
But I can tell you what
you are building towards.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:00.780
A business that doesn't need you stepping
in every five minutes, you getting real

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:05.150
hours back in your week, decisions going
to the right people instead of landing on

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:09.670
your desk, your court processes written
down so someone else can follow them, and

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.190
a proper handle on your
numbers and your cash.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.688
Less than you think. I know time is the
worry, because it's probably why you are

00:03:18.688 --> 00:03:20.620
looking at this in the first place.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.560
In practice, it's a session with me every
couple of weeks, plus some focused work in

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.980
between, and your team carries
as much of that as you do.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.260
I'm not adding another job to your plate.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.780
The whole point is to take work off you.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.750
The time you put in early is what
buys you those hours back later.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.100
That's what the first call is
for, and it works both ways.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.380
30 minutes, and it's not a sales pitch.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:48.860
I'll ask where you are at, and I'll
tell you straight whether I can help.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.900
If I'm not the right person
for what you need, I'll say so.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.820
I'd much rather do that than take
on a client I can't get results for.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:58.420
So I hope that's answered
most of your questions.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.240
If there's anything I haven't covered,
don't worry, on the call I'm happy to go

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.140
into as much detail as you need.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.950
Thanks very much for watching,
and I'll speak to you soon.
